What C++ measures here is NOT what a managed slice measures. A std::string is already
UTF-8, so there is no narrowing transcoder and nothing can fail to be representable:
these rows price WIDTH and VALIDATION, like the rust slice's, and must not be read
across against a .NET or JVM column that prices a transcoder (SHAPES.md).

== the content sets, on whole payloads ==
-std=201703  impl=target  linkage=shared  rounds=9
protobuf 3021012.  Oracle: the INCUMBENT arm, anchored to manifest.json on ascii
C++ holds UTF-8 already, so these rows price WIDTH AND VALIDATION, never a
narrowing transcoder. Not comparable with a managed slice's (SHAPES.md).

